---
title: Pretzel Rolls (CSO)
description: Don't skip the boiling step - it's what gives these rolls their classic pretzel crust.
course: bread
difficulty: medium
cook time: 15 minutes
prep time: 75 minutes
source.author: Sub-Zero Wolf, Mastering the CSO
source.url: https://www.subzero-wolf.com/
tags: CSO, steam
---

= Dough =

In a small pot, heat @milk{1%cup} and @butter{2%tbsp} until warm (110°F).

Pour the melted butter and milk into the bowl of a #stand mixer{}.
Add @brown sugar{2%tbsp}, @instant yeast{1%packet}, @salt{2%tsp}, and @all-purpose flour{2.75%cups}.
Knead on medium-low speed using the dough hook until smooth, about ~{8%minutes}.

Form the dough into a ball and place it in a #lightly greased bowl{}, cover, and let rise for ~{1%hour} or until doubled in size.

= Boiling and Baking =

Place the modular rack in the middle of the #Convection Steam Oven{} (CSO) and preheat to 375°F in Convection Steam mode.

In a #large pot{}, combine @water{3%quarts} and @baking soda{3/4%cup} and bring to a boil.

Divide the dough into 12 equal pieces; gently roll each piece into a ball.
Place dough balls into the boiling solution.
Let them boil for ~{2%minutes}, flipping the balls after 1 minute.
Remove the dough with a slotted spoon and place on a plate.

Generously spray a #perforated pan{} with non-stick spray.
Evenly space the rolls on the pan.

Combine @egg{1}(beaten) and @water{1%tsp} in a small bowl to make an egg wash.
Brush the rolls with egg wash and score the top of each with a sharp knife.
Sprinkle with @coarse salt{}(optional), if desired.

Slide the pan into the preheated oven. Bake until the rolls are well browned, approximately ~{10-12%minutes}.
